00:00:02.070 --> 00:00:03.830 align:start position:0%
the national transportation safety board  determines that the probable cause of  this  accident was the pilot's decision to  continue flight under visual flight  rules  into instrument meteorological  conditions which resulted in the pilot's  spatial disorientation  and loss of control a final word from  the investigation into the helicopter  crash that killed kobe bryant and 13  year old daughter gianna  as well as seven others last january at  a press conference on monday the  national transportation safety board  announced they've completed their full  report on the tragic accident  and that the investigation is now closed  here's what we learned following their  year-long investigation into the tragic  accident the ntsb  said there was no evidence of internal  engine failure in the helicopter  contributing to the accident was the  pilot's likely  self-induced pressure and the pilot's  planned contin  continuation bias which adversely  affected  his decision making and island express  helicopters inadequate review  and oversight of its safety management  processes  robert sumwalt chairman of the ntsb  stated the pilot ara zobian  flew into the clouds a violation of  federal standards  and then likely developed spatial  disorientation  meaning he couldn't interpret the  helicopter's position in relation to the  earth  or any other points of reference we're  talking about  spatial disorientation where literally  the pilot may not know  which way is up or down whether he or  she is leaning  left or right in addition the ntsb noted  there was no evidence that island  express helicopters  or kobe bryant himself were at fault for  zobian agreeing to fly in the  challenging weather conditions that  morning  this could complicate the wrongful death  lawsuit filed by kobe's wife  vanessa bryant in march 2020. the  lawsuit alleges zobian made multiple  errors and that island express  helicopters had  advanced knowledge of his unfitness due  to a previous violation in 2015.  in court documents obtained by e.t  vanessa is asking for substantial  compensation  claiming their family lost hundreds of  millions of dollars in earnings  from kobe's death this solemn update  comes just one day after the bryant  family received some news worth  celebrating  eighteen-year-old daughter of vanessa  and kobe natalia has signed with img  models  the famed talent agency shared the news  on monday and posted a stunning photo of  the bryant's eldest  child in a statement natalia said quote  i have always been interested in fashion  since a very young age i have a love for  the industry and ever since i can  remember  i wanted to model there is a lot to  learn but i feel this is a great  opportunity for me to learn  and express myself creatively proud mom  vanessa quickly shared the post on her  instagram account  writing i'm so happy for you i love you  nani  you
 

